    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\"Carrickroe\" on Howth Baily's favoured Ceanchor Road, enjoys spectacular south facing panoramic views of Dublin Bay. Set well back from Ceanchor Road the house rests on the most elevated part of its site to take full advantage of the breathtaking vista beyond.  \r\n \r\nThis, is Howth's most sought-after address.  Extending to approx. 358.6 sq. m. (3,860 sq. ft.), Carrickroe offers generous proportions , a highly adaptable layout and the perfect balance of formal reception rooms and practical family living space.\r\n \r\nThe accommodation is thoughtfully arranged over two floors with breathtaking views from all south facing rooms. At the lower ground floor level, a spacious hall at the heart of the home leads to an impressive open plan living room with an adjoining sunroom, creating a generous space for both everyday living and entertaining. A separate dining room connects the main living space with the kitchen cum breakfast room, which is complemented by a large utility room, a boot room, a guest WC and a wine cellar. Two substantial double bedrooms are located at this level. One benefits from a walk-in wardrobe, together with a spacious family bathroom. This arrangement offers flexibility for family life and is equally suited to accommodate occasional guests. \r\n \r\nThe elevated split level site allows convenient access to both floors from outside.  The upper floor opens into a bright entrance hall leading to an elevated living room with panoramic views. This living space is one of the properties most coveted features.  The first floor further comprises three generously proportioned bedrooms, including a principal bedroom suite extending to approximately 8.0m x 7.5m with an adjoining en-suite bathroom. Two further bedrooms are served by a second family bathroom off the landing, while a number of useful store rooms are adjacent.  \r\n \r\nThe interior design provides exceptional versatility, allowing the accommodation to adapt effortlessly to changing family needs. Whether accommodating a growing family, providing dedicated work-from-home space or creating separate living areas for extended family, Carrickroe presents a home that is both substantial and remarkably flexible. \r\n\r\nThe generous site is surrounded by mature boundaries with well stocked planted borders. An extensive south facing lawn spans the length of the site from the main outside terrace down towards the entrance gates. This garden and paved terrace provides ample amenity space in a secluded south facing setting with wonderful views. Inside the entrance gate parking for several vehicles is available. A garage is located at the entrance and there is additional parking spaces to the rear of the residence. \r\n \r\nCeanchor Road enjoys a peaceful setting with convenient access to the nearby Howth Village, where an excellent selection of renowned restaurants, cafés, and shops can be found. Howth Harbour, the marina and the famous cliff walks are all close by, offering Howth's finest coastal scenery. Excellent sporting amenities are all within easy reach, while several highly regarded primary and secondary schools serve the area. \r\n \r\nHowth DART Station connects the peninsula to Dublin City, while retaining all the charm and character of coastal village living.\r\n\r\nViewing is available by appointment only with Gallagher Quigley."
      },
